Stellaris version 4.4.* - NOT achievement compatible - English (other languages are available below as unofficial submods)

For a more dynamic and realistic Galactic Community.

Notice: Don't use this version if you're running Ethics and Civics: Bug Branch. Use [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3259721651]this version instead. It is a standalone, you shouldn't use both NGS variants at the same time.

 Mod introduction: 
  ->  This mod offers the player a significantly better Galactic Community experience through vast improvements to AI voting logic (such as more personalized AI weights depending on ethics, civics, origins, etc. or soft cooldowns on sanctions to prevent queue clogging) and also through improvements/additions to the resolutions themselves (such as more balanced resolution modifiers or a wider range of breach conditions for the more extreme resolutions).

  ->  NGS also revives many of the resolutions added by Nemesis, such as the Custodian and the Imperium ones, enabling AI to make much more significant changes to the Galactic Community (You might see AI become Emperor by themselves from time to time as well and actually pass Imperium resolutions accordingly)
        
  ->  In addition to these improvements, this mod doubles the amount of resolutions available to the player, enabling policy enforcement pathways for Authoritarians, Xenophobes, Xenophiles, Megacorps (including criminal ones), and even Gestalts, where previously only Egalitarians, Materialists and Spiritualists had resolution trees tailored for them.

  ->  And as a final bonus, all vanilla resolutions (including those added by this mod) now have a level 6 resolution for even more extremism so that you can impose your will upon the galaxy more efficiently.


 Summary of features: 
New resolutions: 6 new Authoritarian resolutions, 6 new Xenophobe resolutions, 6 new Xenophile resolutions, 6 new Gestalt resolutions, one crystalline protection resolution, 6 new crime resolutions, 6 new corporate crime resolutions, 6 new exploration resolutions, 6 new healthcare resolutions, level 6 resolutions for all regular vanilla categories (with the exception of the Defense Privatization and Suzerains categories), level 4 sanctions, galactic population controls resolution (extreme measure to reduce endgame lag, AI will never propose it);

Reworked Galactic Community: Complete overhaul of most vanilla resolutions for AI weights (AI will vote smarter) and ethic attraction to ethic-based resolutions (such as the greater good ones and the new authoritarian ones). Certain authorities are now banned for the high level authoritarian and egalitarian resolutions and diplomatic weight will be increased/decreased for high-level resolutions - high-level authoritarian resolutions will decrease diplomatic weight for egalitarians and increase it for authoritarians. (I have scripted breach fixes that AI can also use, and combined with the ethics attraction whatever side dominates in diplo weight should be able to change the whole galaxy to adopt their ideologies over time). The senate timer has also been significantly sped up to compensate for the number of resolutions. (360 days for voting, 180 days for recess)

NOTE: It is recommended to have [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1623423360&searchtext=UI+overhaul]UI Overhaul Dynamic installed alongside as it makes the windows bigger and longer text fit inside the blocks.

Compatibility
- Stellaris Evolved: Major Incompatibility - This should be obvious. SE modifies far too many aspects of the game for passive compatibility with NGS, and most other mods;

- Expanded Espionage and Diplomacy: Major Incompatibility - Requires the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2975286025]NGS + EED Compatibility Patch (outdated) ;

- Dawn of the Republic: Medium Incompatibility - Check load order. The nemesis resolution overwrites that NGS does are in direct conflict with those from Dawn of the Republic. NGS must be put below DotR so that my mod can load after it to correctly overwrite files. Not doing so can result in missing/broken resolution categories if the two mods loaded together;

- Ethics and Civics: Classic/Bug Branch: Medium Incompatibility - A variant of NGS fully compatible with Bug Branch is available: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3259721651]NGS: Ethics and Civics Variant

- More Emperor and Custodian Resolutions: Minor/Medium Incompatibility - The developer of MECR has said that their mod has passive compatibility built-in for NGS, however some users have encountered some issues using the two together - Caution is advised;

- Superstates: Minor Incompatibility - A few Custodian resolutions conflict with those from this mod, however you shouldn't encounter any issues;

NOTE: If you encounter a crash while hovering over the Galactic Community icon - it's a mod conflict caused by overwrites from other mods, it's not an issue with NGS.

NGS is currently available in the following languages (you must use both the translation patch and this mod):
- English: Official language of NGS, maintained directly by me - current page;

- Russian: Unofficial translation, maintained by knon_20 - [url=steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3026404123]Russian Extension;

- Simplified Chinese: Unofficial translation, maintained by 南北路多 - [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3710678078]Chinese Extension 

- French: N/A;

- German: N/A;

- Japanese: Unofficial translation, maintained by Rio_Mizuhoshi - [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3123397307]Japanese Extension;

- Korean: N/A;

- Polish: N/A;

- Spanish: N/A;

